docs\reviews\codex-hotfix-A.raw.md:1478:  If tenant 1 previously created and deleted a `zszj` account, this guard still treats that deleted row as an occupied username and permanently skips the demo-account rename. Application username validation and login exclude deleted users through `BaseDO`'s `@TableLogic`, and the shipped PostgreSQL schema has no unique username constraint requiring this restriction. Consequently, no active account is available under the intended new login despite the migration committing successfully. Limit the blocking rows to `deleted = 0`.
